<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Polygon Reduction</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Polygon Reduction</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + D</b></span></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Polygon Reduction</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command reduces points in the visible selected meshes. Unlike sampling,</span> <span class="Command">Polygon Reduction</span> <span lang="EN-GB">works in an intelligent fashion to preserve the shape of the original data set. In areas where surface curvature is high more points are kept, in flatter areas the data is more sparse. This allows the user to reduce the size of a data set while preserving feature lines etc. The resulting data is in mesh format.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../images/polygon_reduction.gif" width="401px" height="284px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Polygon count reduction criteria</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3D distance tolerance</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> decimation removes vertices from areas with less detail than the rest of the selected data set. This option decimates the data using the given number for tolerance. The tolerance represents distance from a point (that will be removed) to the surface formed by the neighbour points excluding the current point. Default value: 0.01mm</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Decrease by</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> decreases the number of triangles in the selected data set by the given percentage. Default value is 50%</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Maximum edge length</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">- decrease the number of triangles of the selected data keeping each triangle edge length up to the given value. Default value is 5mm.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Optimise</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Decimation algorithms are optimising either speed or accuracy. For example, if the slider is on maximum accuracy you will be running the 'preserving features' decimation only, which is rather slow. Default value: optimise by accuracy</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Vertices</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Decimate external</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> allow decimation of triangles on the boundary of the object. This may be undesirable if the boundary quality is important. Default value: checked.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on partial selections or whole entities. If the command is applied for second time on a particular entity, KUBE will offer you to save the file before proceeding.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">that in contrast to the</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="merge.htm">Merge</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">command, where all selected meshes are converted into a one mesh, Polygon Reduction will reduces the polygon number keeping the entities separated.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Polygon Reduction</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to reduce the number of triangles in a mesh while keeping its features unchanged.</span></p>

